WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here at "Late Night"
every night,

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.036 size:78% position:39%
I deliver a monologue
comprised of jokes

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
written by a diverse team
of writers.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.840
As a result, a lot of jokes
come across my desk that,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
due to my being
a straight, white male,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be difficult
for me to deliver.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we don't think that
should stop you

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:15.081
from enjoying those jokes,
so we'd like to share them

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.518
with you now in a segment called
"Jokes Seth Can't Tell."

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:25.291
These are two of our writers,
Amber and Jenny, everybody.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm black.
-And I'm gay.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we're both women.
-And I'm not.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.431 line:92%
So, here's how this works.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll read the setups
for these jokes,

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.635
and Amber and Jenny will read
the punch lines, all right?

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.972
Here we go.
February is Black History Month.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:44.144 size:84% position:42%
-So find a black person
and leave them alone.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.512 line:92%
-At an aquarium in New Zealand,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:49.282
a pair of lesbian penguins
recently welcomed a baby chick.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You could tell
they were lesbians

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they were both
wearing tuxedos.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:58.691 line:92%
-A boy in Indiana called 911

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get help with
his math homework.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:06.599
-That story again --
a white child went unsupervised.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.902 line:92%
-Singer Melissa Etheridge

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
is currently writing songs
for a Broadway musical.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the first known case of
lesbians and gay men

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
being excited
about the same thing.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Martin Luther King Day
was last month.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:27.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he saw his shadow, so
it's 200 more years of racism.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A woman in China
has been diagnosed with

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.395 line:92%
a rare type of hearing loss

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
that prevents her
from hearing male voices.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Said women,
"Oh, please be contagious."

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.971
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Very funny.
Very, very funny. Next joke.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm sorry.
Amber, did you hear something?

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I did not hear anything.
-I know you can hear me.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course we can hear you.
You have a lady voice.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do not!

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.551 line:92%
"BlacKkKlansman" was nominated

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
for an Academy Award
for Best Picture.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:06.025
-And white Klansman was
nominated for attorney general.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.532
-According to a recent study,
the number of British people

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.535
identifying as lesbians has gone
up in the last five years.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:21.241
-Lesbians or, as they call them
in Britain, crumpet munchers.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A Texas sheriff has
placed cardboard cutouts

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.715 line:92%
of officers holding radar guns

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.184
on the side of
several roads to deter speeding.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:37.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And even one of those
managed to shoot a black guy.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They said, "What?!"
-I don't know.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:42.795
-Why don't you tell one?
-I don't think I want to.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.563 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I think you should.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like if I tell one,
it won't end well.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:49.369
-Oh, just one.
-All right, all right. Just one.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:53.006
"Black Panther" recently won
the SAG Award for Best Ensemble.

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What's an ensemble?",
said lesbians getting dressed.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:03:00.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How dare you?!
-You told me it would be okay.

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You should the be
ashamed of yourself!

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Black women and lesbians
are liars!

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:08.288 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.923 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We'll be right back.

